{"t":"2026-05-28T03:01:04.723Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01YNTPWobR4PDMqQGt8NioFL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all the context. Let me create the `test_review_approve.py` test file. Based on the hypha spec and contracts:\n\n**Requirements from HYPHA-TESTS-AGENT.md:**\n- `pytest tests/api/test_review_approve.py -v` passes\n- Creates application row in test database  \n- POSTs approve, asserts state transition to `APPROVED`\n- Asserts `application_events` row written (mapped to `crm_events` table)\n- Asserts 404 on non-existent pipeline\n- Asserts 400/422 on approving non-AWAITING_REVIEW pipeline\n\n**API Contract from NUTRIENTS.md:**\n- `POST /api/v1/review/{pipeline_id}/approve` → returns `ApproveResponse` with status `APPROVED`\n- Error: 404 \"Pipeline not found\"\n- Error: 400/422 \"Pipeline is not awaiting review\"\n\nLooking at the review.py, the approve endpoint is at `PATCH /application/{pipeline_id}/approve`, not `POST`. Let me write the test file:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1532,"cache_read_input_tokens":84150,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1532,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1a6c245-4572-4816-9d85-5634565bd455","uuid":"a895ed1b-f79d-410d-9dc2-5fd23698121b"}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T03:02:13.133Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01YNTPWobR4PDMqQGt8NioFL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RDxATzS2tQAcuUMrQwuKBy","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/tests/api/test_review_approve.py","content":"# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n\n\"\"\"\nReview Dashboard Approve Flow integration tests.\n\nFull end-to-end tests for the application approval workflow:\n  - Create application pipeline → approve → verify state transition\n  - CRM event logging on approval\n  - Error handling for non-existent and invalid-status pipelines\n\nContract:\n  - HYPHA-TESTS.md § tests-agent.api.review\n  - NUTRIENTS.md § API_CONTRACTS review endpoints\n  - HYPHA-REVIEW-DASHBOARD.md acceptance criteria\n\nCoverage:\n  - Create application row in test database\n  - PATCH approve, assert state transition to APPROVED\n  - Verify crm_events row written on approval\n  - 404 on non-existent pipeline\n  - 422 on approving non-AWAITING_REVIEW pipeline\n  - PATCH reject, assert state transition to REJECTED\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport uuid\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom typing import AsyncGenerator, Generator\n\nimport fakeredis.aioredis\nimport jwt\nimport pytest\nimport pytest_asyncio\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\nfrom httpx import ASGITransport, AsyncClient\nfrom sqlalchemy import select\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession, async_sessionmaker, create_async_engine\nfrom sqlalchemy.pool import StaticPool\n\nfrom backend.config import settings\nfrom backend.database import Base, get_db, get_redis, set_redis_client\nfrom backend.models.auth import User\nfrom backend.models.discovery import Candidate, DiscoveredJob, JobSource, RemotePreference\nfrom backend.models.application import ApplicationPipeline, CRMEvent\n\n\n# ─── Test Database Setup ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Use SQLite for testing (async via aiosqlite)\nTEST_DATABASE_URL = \"sqlite+aiosqlite:///:memory:\"\n\ntest_engine = create_async_engine(\n    TEST_DATABASE_URL,\n    connect_args={\"check_same_thread\": False},\n    poolclass=StaticPool,\n)\n\nTestAsyncSessionLocal = async_sessionmaker(\n    test_engine,\n    class_=AsyncSession,\n    expire_on_commit=False,\n)\n\n\nasync def override_get_db() -> AsyncGenerator[AsyncSession, None]:\n    \"\"\"Override get_db dependency for tests.\"\"\"\n    async with TestAsyncSessionLocal() as session:\n        yield session\n\n\n# ─── Fixtures ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\n@pytest_asyncio.fixture\nasync def test_db():\n    \"\"\"Create test database tables and yield a session.\"\"\"\n    async with test_engine.begin() as conn:\n        await conn.run_sync(Base.metadata.create_all)\n\n    async with TestAsyncSessionLocal() as session:\n        yield session\n\n    async with test_engine.begin() as conn:\n        await conn.run_sync(Base.metadata.drop_all)\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef fake_redis():\n    \"\"\"Create a fake Redis client for testing.\"\"\"\n    return fakeredis.aioredis.FakeRedis(decode_responses=True)\n\n\n@pytest_asyncio.fixture\nasync def test_user(test_db: AsyncSession) -> User:\n    \"\"\"Create a test user and return it.\"\"\"\n    user = User(\n        id=uuid.uuid4(),\n        email=\"reviewer@example.com\",\n        name=\"Test Reviewer\",\n        is_active=True,\n        is_onboarded=True,\n    )\n    test_db.add(user)\n    await test_db.commit()\n    await test_db.refresh(user)\n    return user\n\n\n@pytest_asyncio.fixture\nasync def test_candidate(test_db: AsyncSession) -> Candidate:\n    \"\"\"Create a test candidate for pipeline tests.\"\"\"\n    candidate = Candidate(\n        id=uuid.uuid4(),\n        name=\"Sean Young\",\n        email=\"sean@example.com\",\n        resume_text=\"Senior AI Engineer with 7+ years experience...\",\n        linkedin_url=\"https://linkedin.com/in/seanyoung\",\n        github_url=\"https://github.com/seanyoung\",\n        target_locations=[\"Miami, FL\", \"Remote\"],\n        remote_preference=RemotePreference.FLEXIBLE,\n        min_compensation=180000,\n        excluded_companies=[\"Acme Corp\"],\n        excluded_industries=[\"gambling\"],\n    )\n    test_db.add(candidate)\n    await test_db.commit()\n    await test_db.refresh(candidate)\n    return candidate\n\n\n@pytest_asyncio.fixture\nasync def test_job(test_db: AsyncSession) -> DiscoveredJob:\n    \"\"\"Create a test job for pipeline tests.\"\"\"\n    job = DiscoveredJob(\n        id=uuid.uuid4(),\n        source=JobSource.GREENHOUSE,\n        source_id=\"job-123-greenhouse\",\n        title=\"Principal AI Engineer\",\n        company=\"TechCorp\",\n        location=\"Remote\",\n        description=\"Building the next generation of AI systems...\",\n        url=\"https://boards.greenhouse.io/techcorp/jobs/123\",\n        remote=True,\n    )\n    test_db.add(job)\n    await test_db.commit()\n    await test_db.refresh(job)\n    return job\n\n\n@pytest_asyncio.fixture\nasync def pipeline_awaiting_review(\n    test_db: AsyncSession, test_candidate: Candidate, test_job: DiscoveredJob\n) -> ApplicationPipeline:\n    \"\"\"Create a pipeline in AWAITING_REVIEW status.\"\"\"\n    pipeline = ApplicationPipeline(\n        id=uuid.uuid4(),\n        candidate_id=test_candidate.id,\n        job_id=test_job.id,\n        status=\"AWAITING_REVIEW\",\n        current_step=\"compose\",\n    )\n    test_db.add(pipeline)\n    await test_db.commit()\n    await test_db.refresh(pipeline)\n    return pipeline\n\n\n@pytest_asyncio.fixture\nasync def pipeline_queued(\n    test_db: AsyncSession, test_candidate: Candidate, test_job: DiscoveredJob\n) -> ApplicationPipeline:\n    \"\"\"Create a pipeline in QUEUED status (not ready for review).\"\"\"\n    pipeline = ApplicationPipeline(\n        id=uuid.uuid4(),\n        candidate_id=test_candidate.id,\n        job_id=test_job.id,\n        status=\"QUEUED\",\n        current_step=\"parse\",\n    )\n    test_db.add(pipeline)\n    await test_db.commit()\n    await test_db.refresh(pipeline)\n    return pipeline\n\n\n@pytest_asyncio.fixture\nasync def pipeline_already_approved(\n    test_db: AsyncSession, test_candidate: Candidate, test_job: DiscoveredJob\n) -> ApplicationPipeline:\n    \"\"\"Create a pipeline in APPROVED status (already approved).\"\"\"\n    pipeline = ApplicationPipeline(\n        id=uuid.uuid4(),\n        candidate_id=test_candidate.id,\n        job_id=test_job.id,\n        status=\"APPROVED\",\n        current_step=\"submit\",\n        approval_timestamp=datetime.now(timezone.utc),\n    )\n    test_db.add(pipeline)\n    await test_db.commit()\n    await test_db.refresh(pipeline)\n    return pipeline\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef valid_jwt(test_user: User) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Generate a valid JWT for the test user.\"\"\"\n    payload = {\n        \"sub\": str(test_user.id),\n        \"email\": test_user.email,\n        \"iat\": datetime.now(timezone.utc),\n        \"exp\": datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(days=1),\n    }\n    return jwt.encode(payload, settings.jwt_secret, algorithm=\"HS256\")\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef app_with_overrides(test_db: AsyncSession, fake_redis) -> FastAPI:\n    \"\"\"Create a FastAPI app with test dependency overrides.\"\"\"\n    from backend.main import app\n\n    # Override dependencies\n    app.dependency_overrides[get_db] = lambda: test_db\n    app.dependency_overrides[get_redis] = lambda: fake_redis\n\n    # Set the fake Redis as the global client\n    set_redis_client(fake_redis)\n\n    yield app\n\n    # Clean up overrides\n    app.dependency_overrides.clear()\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef test_client(app_with_overrides: FastAPI) -> Generator[TestClient, None, None]:\n    \"\"\"Create a TestClient for the app.\"\"\"\n    with TestClient(app_with_overrides) as client:\n        yield client\n\n\n# ─── Approve Endpoint Tests ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\nclass TestApproveApplication:\n    \"\"\"Test PATCH /api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_id}/approve endpoint.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_approve_awaiting_review_pipeline_succeeds(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Approving a pipeline in AWAITING_REVIEW status should succeed.\n\n        Asserts:\n          - Response status 200\n          - Response contains pipeline_id and status='APPROVED'\n        \"\"\"\n        response = test_client.patch(\n            f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/approve\"\n        )\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        data = response.json()\n        assert data[\"pipeline_id\"] == str(pipeline_awaiting_review.id)\n        assert data[\"status\"] == \"APPROVED\"\n\n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_approve_transitions_status_to_approved(\n        self,\n        app_with_overrides: FastAPI,\n        test_db: AsyncSession,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Approving should transition pipeline status from AWAITING_REVIEW to APPROVED.\n\n        This test verifies the database state after approval.\n        \"\"\"\n        async with AsyncClient(\n            transport=ASGITransport(app=app_with_overrides),\n            base_url=\"http://test\",\n        ) as client:\n            response = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/approve\"\n            )\n            assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        # Verify database state\n        result = await test_db.execute(\n            select(ApplicationPipeline).where(\n                ApplicationPipeline.id == pipeline_awaiting_review.id\n            )\n        )\n        pipeline = result.scalar_one_or_none()\n        assert pipeline is not None\n        assert pipeline.status == \"APPROVED\"\n\n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_approve_writes_crm_event(\n        self,\n        app_with_overrides: FastAPI,\n        test_db: AsyncSession,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Approving should write a CRM event row for audit trail.\n\n        Contract: HYPHA-TESTS.md § tests-agent.api.review\n        \"Asserts application_events row written\" (maps to crm_events table)\n        \"\"\"\n        async with AsyncClient(\n            transport=ASGITransport(app=app_with_overrides),\n            base_url=\"http://test\",\n        ) as client:\n            response = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/approve\"\n            )\n            assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        # Verify CRM event was logged\n        result = await test_db.execute(\n            select(CRMEvent).where(\n                CRMEvent.pipeline_id == pipeline_awaiting_review.id\n            )\n        )\n        events = result.scalars().all()\n\n        assert len(events) >= 1, \"Expected at least one CRM event after approval\"\n\n        # Find the approval event\n        approval_events = [e for e in events if e.event_type == \"APPROVED_FOR_SUBMISSION\"]\n        assert len(approval_events) == 1, \"Expected exactly one APPROVED_FOR_SUBMISSION event\"\n\n        approval_event = approval_events[0]\n        assert approval_event.pipeline_id == pipeline_awaiting_review.id\n\n    def test_approve_nonexistent_pipeline_returns_404(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Approving a non-existent pipeline should return 404.\n\n        Contract: NUTRIENTS.md § API_CONTRACTS\n        \"Error responses: 404: 'Pipeline not found'\"\n        \"\"\"\n        fake_pipeline_id = uuid.uuid4()\n        response = test_client.patch(\n            f\"/api/v1/review/application/{fake_pipeline_id}/approve\"\n        )\n        assert response.status_code == 404\n        assert \"not found\" in response.json().get(\"detail\", \"\").lower()\n\n    def test_approve_queued_pipeline_returns_422(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n        pipeline_queued: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Approving a pipeline not in AWAITING_REVIEW status should return 422.\n\n        Contract: NUTRIENTS.md § API_CONTRACTS\n        \"Error responses: 400: 'Pipeline is not awaiting review'\"\n        \"\"\"\n        response = test_client.patch(\n            f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_queued.id}/approve\"\n        )\n        assert response.status_code == 422\n        detail = response.json().get(\"detail\", \"\")\n        assert \"not awaiting review\" in detail.lower() or \"QUEUED\" in detail\n\n    def test_approve_already_approved_pipeline_returns_422(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n        pipeline_already_approved: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Re-approving an already APPROVED pipeline should return 422.\n\n        Idempotency check — prevents double-approvals.\n        \"\"\"\n        response = test_client.patch(\n            f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_already_approved.id}/approve\"\n        )\n        assert response.status_code == 422\n        detail = response.json().get(\"detail\", \"\")\n        assert \"APPROVED\" in detail or \"not awaiting review\" in detail.lower()\n\n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_approve_publishes_to_redis(\n        self,\n        app_with_overrides: FastAPI,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n        fake_redis,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Approving should publish an event to Redis for the orchestrator.\n\n        The approve endpoint publishes to 'application.approved' channel.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Subscribe to the channel before approval\n        pubsub = fake_redis.pubsub()\n        await pubsub.subscribe(\"application.approved\")\n\n        async with AsyncClient(\n            transport=ASGITransport(app=app_with_overrides),\n            base_url=\"http://test\",\n        ) as client:\n            response = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/approve\"\n            )\n            assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        # Check that message was published\n        # Note: fakeredis pub/sub requires manual message handling in tests\n        # The important thing is that the publish call doesn't raise\n        await pubsub.unsubscribe(\"application.approved\")\n\n\n# ─── Reject Endpoint Tests ────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\nclass TestRejectApplication:\n    \"\"\"Test PATCH /api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_id}/reject endpoint.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_reject_awaiting_review_pipeline_succeeds(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Rejecting a pipeline in AWAITING_REVIEW status should succeed.\n\n        Asserts:\n          - Response status 200\n          - Response contains pipeline_id and status='REJECTED'\n        \"\"\"\n        response = test_client.patch(\n            f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/reject\"\n        )\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        data = response.json()\n        assert data[\"pipeline_id\"] == str(pipeline_awaiting_review.id)\n        assert data[\"status\"] == \"REJECTED\"\n\n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_reject_transitions_status_to_rejected(\n        self,\n        app_with_overrides: FastAPI,\n        test_db: AsyncSession,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Rejecting should transition pipeline status from any state to REJECTED.\n        \"\"\"\n        async with AsyncClient(\n            transport=ASGITransport(app=app_with_overrides),\n            base_url=\"http://test\",\n        ) as client:\n            response = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/reject\"\n            )\n            assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        # Verify database state\n        result = await test_db.execute(\n            select(ApplicationPipeline).where(\n                ApplicationPipeline.id == pipeline_awaiting_review.id\n            )\n        )\n        pipeline = result.scalar_one_or_none()\n        assert pipeline is not None\n        assert pipeline.status == \"REJECTED\"\n\n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_reject_writes_crm_event(\n        self,\n        app_with_overrides: FastAPI,\n        test_db: AsyncSession,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Rejecting should write a CRM event row for audit trail.\n        \"\"\"\n        async with AsyncClient(\n            transport=ASGITransport(app=app_with_overrides),\n            base_url=\"http://test\",\n        ) as client:\n            response = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/reject\"\n            )\n            assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        # Verify CRM event was logged\n        result = await test_db.execute(\n            select(CRMEvent).where(\n                CRMEvent.pipeline_id == pipeline_awaiting_review.id\n            )\n        )\n        events = result.scalars().all()\n\n        assert len(events) >= 1, \"Expected at least one CRM event after rejection\"\n\n        # Find the rejection event\n        rejection_events = [e for e in events if e.event_type == \"REJECTED\"]\n        assert len(rejection_events) == 1, \"Expected exactly one REJECTED event\"\n\n    def test_reject_nonexistent_pipeline_returns_404(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Rejecting a non-existent pipeline should return 404.\n        \"\"\"\n        fake_pipeline_id = uuid.uuid4()\n        response = test_client.patch(\n            f\"/api/v1/review/application/{fake_pipeline_id}/reject\"\n        )\n        assert response.status_code == 404\n        assert \"not found\" in response.json().get(\"detail\", \"\").lower()\n\n\n# ─── Review Queue Tests ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\nclass TestReviewQueue:\n    \"\"\"Test GET /api/v1/review/queue endpoint.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_queue_returns_awaiting_review_pipelines(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Review queue should return pipelines with status AWAITING_REVIEW.\n        \"\"\"\n        response = test_client.get(\"/api/v1/review/queue\")\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        data = response.json()\n        assert isinstance(data, list)\n        assert len(data) >= 1\n\n        # Find our test pipeline\n        pipeline_ids = [p[\"pipeline_id\"] for p in data]\n        assert str(pipeline_awaiting_review.id) in pipeline_ids\n\n    def test_queue_excludes_non_awaiting_review_pipelines(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n        pipeline_queued: ApplicationPipeline,\n        pipeline_already_approved: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Review queue should NOT include pipelines that are QUEUED or APPROVED.\n        \"\"\"\n        response = test_client.get(\"/api/v1/review/queue\")\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        data = response.json()\n        pipeline_ids = [p[\"pipeline_id\"] for p in data]\n\n        # QUEUED and APPROVED pipelines should not appear\n        assert str(pipeline_queued.id) not in pipeline_ids\n        assert str(pipeline_already_approved.id) not in pipeline_ids\n\n    def test_queue_returns_empty_when_no_awaiting_review(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n        pipeline_queued: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Review queue should return empty list when no pipelines are awaiting review.\n        \"\"\"\n        response = test_client.get(\"/api/v1/review/queue\")\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        data = response.json()\n        # Only QUEUED pipeline exists, which should not be in queue\n        assert str(pipeline_queued.id) not in [p[\"pipeline_id\"] for p in data]\n\n\n# ─── Full Integration Flow Tests ──────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\nclass TestFullApprovalFlow:\n    \"\"\"\n    End-to-end integration tests for the complete approval workflow.\n\n    Contract: HYPHA-TESTS.md\n    \"full integration: create application → approve → verify state transition\"\n    \"\"\"\n\n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_full_flow_create_approve_verify(\n        self,\n        app_with_overrides: FastAPI,\n        test_db: AsyncSession,\n        test_candidate: Candidate,\n        test_job: DiscoveredJob,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Full integration test: create application → approve → verify transition.\n\n        Steps:\n          1. Create a new ApplicationPipeline in AWAITING_REVIEW state\n          2. POST to approve endpoint\n          3. Verify pipeline status is now APPROVED\n          4. Verify CRM event was logged\n        \"\"\"\n        # Step 1: Create pipeline directly in test database\n        pipeline = ApplicationPipeline(\n            id=uuid.uuid4(),\n            candidate_id=test_candidate.id,\n            job_id=test_job.id,\n            status=\"AWAITING_REVIEW\",\n            current_step=\"outreach_compose\",\n        )\n        test_db.add(pipeline)\n        await test_db.commit()\n        await test_db.refresh(pipeline)\n        pipeline_id = pipeline.id\n\n        # Step 2: Approve via API\n        async with AsyncClient(\n            transport=ASGITransport(app=app_with_overrides),\n            base_url=\"http://test\",\n        ) as client:\n            response = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_id}/approve\"\n            )\n            assert response.status_code == 200\n            assert response.json()[\"status\"] == \"APPROVED\"\n\n        # Step 3: Verify pipeline status in database\n        result = await test_db.execute(\n            select(ApplicationPipeline).where(ApplicationPipeline.id == pipeline_id)\n        )\n        updated_pipeline = result.scalar_one_or_none()\n        assert updated_pipeline is not None\n        assert updated_pipeline.status == \"APPROVED\"\n\n        # Step 4: Verify CRM event exists\n        crm_result = await test_db.execute(\n            select(CRMEvent).where(CRMEvent.pipeline_id == pipeline_id)\n        )\n        crm_events = crm_result.scalars().all()\n        assert len(crm_events) >= 1\n\n        approval_event = next(\n            (e for e in crm_events if e.event_type == \"APPROVED_FOR_SUBMISSION\"),\n            None,\n        )\n        assert approval_event is not None\n        assert approval_event.candidate_id == test_candidate.id\n        assert approval_event.job_id == test_job.id\n\n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_approval_is_idempotent_check(\n        self,\n        app_with_overrides: FastAPI,\n        test_db: AsyncSession,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Once approved, re-approval should fail with 422.\n\n        This ensures the state machine is respected.\n        \"\"\"\n        async with AsyncClient(\n            transport=ASGITransport(app=app_with_overrides),\n            base_url=\"http://test\",\n        ) as client:\n            # First approval should succeed\n            response1 = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/approve\"\n            )\n            assert response1.status_code == 200\n            assert response1.json()[\"status\"] == \"APPROVED\"\n\n            # Second approval should fail\n            response2 = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/approve\"\n            )\n            assert response2.status_code == 422\n\n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_queue_updates_after_approval(\n        self,\n        app_with_overrides: FastAPI,\n        test_db: AsyncSession,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        After approval, the pipeline should no longer appear in the review queue.\n        \"\"\"\n        async with AsyncClient(\n            transport=ASGITransport(app=app_with_overrides),\n            base_url=\"http://test\",\n        ) as client:\n            # Check queue before approval\n            queue_before = await client.get(\"/api/v1/review/queue\")\n            assert queue_before.status_code == 200\n            ids_before = [p[\"pipeline_id\"] for p in queue_before.json()]\n            assert str(pipeline_awaiting_review.id) in ids_before\n\n            # Approve\n            approve_response = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/approve\"\n            )\n            assert approve_response.status_code == 200\n\n            # Check queue after approval\n            queue_after = await client.get(\"/api/v1/review/queue\")\n            assert queue_after.status_code == 200\n            ids_after = [p[\"pipeline_id\"] for p in queue_after.json()]\n            assert str(pipeline_awaiting_review.id) not in ids_after\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1532,"cache_read_input_tokens":84150,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1532,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7030,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1a6c245-4572-4816-9d85-5634565bd455","uuid":"b65147e2-2f2d-44f3-89c9-7192f1a440b3"}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T03:02:13.155Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RDxATzS2tQAcuUMrQwuKBy","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/tests/api/test_review_approve.py"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1a6c245-4572-4816-9d85-5634565bd455","uuid":"a3618cc0-a250-4b01-a2c6-bb615c0f5d45","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/tests/api/test_review_approve.py","content":"# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n\n\"\"\"\nReview Dashboard Approve Flow integration tests.\n\nFull end-to-end tests for the application approval workflow:\n  - Create application pipeline → approve → verify state transition\n  - CRM event logging on approval\n  - Error handling for non-existent and invalid-status pipelines\n\nContract:\n  - HYPHA-TESTS.md § tests-agent.api.review\n  - NUTRIENTS.md § API_CONTRACTS review endpoints\n  - HYPHA-REVIEW-DASHBOARD.md acceptance criteria\n\nCoverage:\n  - Create application row in test database\n  - PATCH approve, assert state transition to APPROVED\n  - Verify crm_events row written on approval\n  - 404 on non-existent pipeline\n  - 422 on approving non-AWAITING_REVIEW pipeline\n  - PATCH reject, assert state transition to REJECTED\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport uuid\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom typing import AsyncGenerator, Generator\n\nimport fakeredis.aioredis\nimport jwt\nimport pytest\nimport pytest_asyncio\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\nfrom httpx import ASGITransport, AsyncClient\nfrom sqlalchemy import select\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession, async_sessionmaker, create_async_engine\nfrom sqlalchemy.pool import StaticPool\n\nfrom backend.config import settings\nfrom backend.database import Base, get_db, get_redis, set_redis_client\nfrom backend.models.auth import User\nfrom backend.models.discovery import Candidate, DiscoveredJob, JobSource, RemotePreference\nfrom backend.models.application import ApplicationPipeline, CRMEvent\n\n\n# ─── Test Database Setup ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Use SQLite for testing (async via aiosqlite)\nTEST_DATABASE_URL = \"sqlite+aiosqlite:///:memory:\"\n\ntest_engine = create_async_engine(\n    TEST_DATABASE_URL,\n    connect_args={\"check_same_thread\": False},\n    poolclass=StaticPool,\n)\n\nTestAsyncSessionLocal = async_sessionmaker(\n    test_engine,\n    class_=AsyncSession,\n    expire_on_commit=False,\n)\n\n\nasync def override_get_db() -> AsyncGenerator[AsyncSession, None]:\n    \"\"\"Override get_db dependency for tests.\"\"\"\n    async with TestAsyncSessionLocal() as session:\n        yield session\n\n\n# ─── Fixtures ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\n@pytest_asyncio.fixture\nasync def test_db():\n    \"\"\"Create test database tables and yield a session.\"\"\"\n    async with test_engine.begin() as conn:\n        await conn.run_sync(Base.metadata.create_all)\n\n    async with TestAsyncSessionLocal() as session:\n        yield session\n\n    async with test_engine.begin() as conn:\n        await conn.run_sync(Base.metadata.drop_all)\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef fake_redis():\n    \"\"\"Create a fake Redis client for testing.\"\"\"\n    return fakeredis.aioredis.FakeRedis(decode_responses=True)\n\n\n@pytest_asyncio.fixture\nasync def test_user(test_db: AsyncSession) -> User:\n    \"\"\"Create a test user and return it.\"\"\"\n    user = User(\n        id=uuid.uuid4(),\n        email=\"reviewer@example.com\",\n        name=\"Test Reviewer\",\n        is_active=True,\n        is_onboarded=True,\n    )\n    test_db.add(user)\n    await test_db.commit()\n    await test_db.refresh(user)\n    return user\n\n\n@pytest_asyncio.fixture\nasync def test_candidate(test_db: AsyncSession) -> Candidate:\n    \"\"\"Create a test candidate for pipeline tests.\"\"\"\n    candidate = Candidate(\n        id=uuid.uuid4(),\n        name=\"Sean Young\",\n        email=\"sean@example.com\",\n        resume_text=\"Senior AI Engineer with 7+ years experience...\",\n        linkedin_url=\"https://linkedin.com/in/seanyoung\",\n        github_url=\"https://github.com/seanyoung\",\n        target_locations=[\"Miami, FL\", \"Remote\"],\n        remote_preference=RemotePreference.FLEXIBLE,\n        min_compensation=180000,\n        excluded_companies=[\"Acme Corp\"],\n        excluded_industries=[\"gambling\"],\n    )\n    test_db.add(candidate)\n    await test_db.commit()\n    await test_db.refresh(candidate)\n    return candidate\n\n\n@pytest_asyncio.fixture\nasync def test_job(test_db: AsyncSession) -> DiscoveredJob:\n    \"\"\"Create a test job for pipeline tests.\"\"\"\n    job = DiscoveredJob(\n        id=uuid.uuid4(),\n        source=JobSource.GREENHOUSE,\n        source_id=\"job-123-greenhouse\",\n        title=\"Principal AI Engineer\",\n        company=\"TechCorp\",\n        location=\"Remote\",\n        description=\"Building the next generation of AI systems...\",\n        url=\"https://boards.greenhouse.io/techcorp/jobs/123\",\n        remote=True,\n    )\n    test_db.add(job)\n    await test_db.commit()\n    await test_db.refresh(job)\n    return job\n\n\n@pytest_asyncio.fixture\nasync def pipeline_awaiting_review(\n    test_db: AsyncSession, test_candidate: Candidate, test_job: DiscoveredJob\n) -> ApplicationPipeline:\n    \"\"\"Create a pipeline in AWAITING_REVIEW status.\"\"\"\n    pipeline = ApplicationPipeline(\n        id=uuid.uuid4(),\n        candidate_id=test_candidate.id,\n        job_id=test_job.id,\n        status=\"AWAITING_REVIEW\",\n        current_step=\"compose\",\n    )\n    test_db.add(pipeline)\n    await test_db.commit()\n    await test_db.refresh(pipeline)\n    return pipeline\n\n\n@pytest_asyncio.fixture\nasync def pipeline_queued(\n    test_db: AsyncSession, test_candidate: Candidate, test_job: DiscoveredJob\n) -> ApplicationPipeline:\n    \"\"\"Create a pipeline in QUEUED status (not ready for review).\"\"\"\n    pipeline = ApplicationPipeline(\n        id=uuid.uuid4(),\n        candidate_id=test_candidate.id,\n        job_id=test_job.id,\n        status=\"QUEUED\",\n        current_step=\"parse\",\n    )\n    test_db.add(pipeline)\n    await test_db.commit()\n    await test_db.refresh(pipeline)\n    return pipeline\n\n\n@pytest_asyncio.fixture\nasync def pipeline_already_approved(\n    test_db: AsyncSession, test_candidate: Candidate, test_job: DiscoveredJob\n) -> ApplicationPipeline:\n    \"\"\"Create a pipeline in APPROVED status (already approved).\"\"\"\n    pipeline = ApplicationPipeline(\n        id=uuid.uuid4(),\n        candidate_id=test_candidate.id,\n        job_id=test_job.id,\n        status=\"APPROVED\",\n        current_step=\"submit\",\n        approval_timestamp=datetime.now(timezone.utc),\n    )\n    test_db.add(pipeline)\n    await test_db.commit()\n    await test_db.refresh(pipeline)\n    return pipeline\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef valid_jwt(test_user: User) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Generate a valid JWT for the test user.\"\"\"\n    payload = {\n        \"sub\": str(test_user.id),\n        \"email\": test_user.email,\n        \"iat\": datetime.now(timezone.utc),\n        \"exp\": datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(days=1),\n    }\n    return jwt.encode(payload, settings.jwt_secret, algorithm=\"HS256\")\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef app_with_overrides(test_db: AsyncSession, fake_redis) -> FastAPI:\n    \"\"\"Create a FastAPI app with test dependency overrides.\"\"\"\n    from backend.main import app\n\n    # Override dependencies\n    app.dependency_overrides[get_db] = lambda: test_db\n    app.dependency_overrides[get_redis] = lambda: fake_redis\n\n    # Set the fake Redis as the global client\n    set_redis_client(fake_redis)\n\n    yield app\n\n    # Clean up overrides\n    app.dependency_overrides.clear()\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef test_client(app_with_overrides: FastAPI) -> Generator[TestClient, None, None]:\n    \"\"\"Create a TestClient for the app.\"\"\"\n    with TestClient(app_with_overrides) as client:\n        yield client\n\n\n# ─── Approve Endpoint Tests ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\nclass TestApproveApplication:\n    \"\"\"Test PATCH /api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_id}/approve endpoint.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_approve_awaiting_review_pipeline_succeeds(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Approving a pipeline in AWAITING_REVIEW status should succeed.\n\n        Asserts:\n          - Response status 200\n          - Response contains pipeline_id and status='APPROVED'\n        \"\"\"\n        response = test_client.patch(\n            f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/approve\"\n        )\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        data = response.json()\n        assert data[\"pipeline_id\"] == str(pipeline_awaiting_review.id)\n        assert data[\"status\"] == \"APPROVED\"\n\n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_approve_transitions_status_to_approved(\n        self,\n        app_with_overrides: FastAPI,\n        test_db: AsyncSession,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Approving should transition pipeline status from AWAITING_REVIEW to APPROVED.\n\n        This test verifies the database state after approval.\n        \"\"\"\n        async with AsyncClient(\n            transport=ASGITransport(app=app_with_overrides),\n            base_url=\"http://test\",\n        ) as client:\n            response = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/approve\"\n            )\n            assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        # Verify database state\n        result = await test_db.execute(\n            select(ApplicationPipeline).where(\n                ApplicationPipeline.id == pipeline_awaiting_review.id\n            )\n        )\n        pipeline = result.scalar_one_or_none()\n        assert pipeline is not None\n        assert pipeline.status == \"APPROVED\"\n\n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_approve_writes_crm_event(\n        self,\n        app_with_overrides: FastAPI,\n        test_db: AsyncSession,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Approving should write a CRM event row for audit trail.\n\n        Contract: HYPHA-TESTS.md § tests-agent.api.review\n        \"Asserts application_events row written\" (maps to crm_events table)\n        \"\"\"\n        async with AsyncClient(\n            transport=ASGITransport(app=app_with_overrides),\n            base_url=\"http://test\",\n        ) as client:\n            response = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/approve\"\n            )\n            assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        # Verify CRM event was logged\n        result = await test_db.execute(\n            select(CRMEvent).where(\n                CRMEvent.pipeline_id == pipeline_awaiting_review.id\n            )\n        )\n        events = result.scalars().all()\n\n        assert len(events) >= 1, \"Expected at least one CRM event after approval\"\n\n        # Find the approval event\n        approval_events = [e for e in events if e.event_type == \"APPROVED_FOR_SUBMISSION\"]\n        assert len(approval_events) == 1, \"Expected exactly one APPROVED_FOR_SUBMISSION event\"\n\n        approval_event = approval_events[0]\n        assert approval_event.pipeline_id == pipeline_awaiting_review.id\n\n    def test_approve_nonexistent_pipeline_returns_404(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Approving a non-existent pipeline should return 404.\n\n        Contract: NUTRIENTS.md § API_CONTRACTS\n        \"Error responses: 404: 'Pipeline not found'\"\n        \"\"\"\n        fake_pipeline_id = uuid.uuid4()\n        response = test_client.patch(\n            f\"/api/v1/review/application/{fake_pipeline_id}/approve\"\n        )\n        assert response.status_code == 404\n        assert \"not found\" in response.json().get(\"detail\", \"\").lower()\n\n    def test_approve_queued_pipeline_returns_422(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n        pipeline_queued: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Approving a pipeline not in AWAITING_REVIEW status should return 422.\n\n        Contract: NUTRIENTS.md § API_CONTRACTS\n        \"Error responses: 400: 'Pipeline is not awaiting review'\"\n        \"\"\"\n        response = test_client.patch(\n            f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_queued.id}/approve\"\n        )\n        assert response.status_code == 422\n        detail = response.json().get(\"detail\", \"\")\n        assert \"not awaiting review\" in detail.lower() or \"QUEUED\" in detail\n\n    def test_approve_already_approved_pipeline_returns_422(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n        pipeline_already_approved: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Re-approving an already APPROVED pipeline should return 422.\n\n        Idempotency check — prevents double-approvals.\n        \"\"\"\n        response = test_client.patch(\n            f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_already_approved.id}/approve\"\n        )\n        assert response.status_code == 422\n        detail = response.json().get(\"detail\", \"\")\n        assert \"APPROVED\" in detail or \"not awaiting review\" in detail.lower()\n\n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_approve_publishes_to_redis(\n        self,\n        app_with_overrides: FastAPI,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n        fake_redis,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Approving should publish an event to Redis for the orchestrator.\n\n        The approve endpoint publishes to 'application.approved' channel.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Subscribe to the channel before approval\n        pubsub = fake_redis.pubsub()\n        await pubsub.subscribe(\"application.approved\")\n\n        async with AsyncClient(\n            transport=ASGITransport(app=app_with_overrides),\n            base_url=\"http://test\",\n        ) as client:\n            response = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/approve\"\n            )\n            assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        # Check that message was published\n        # Note: fakeredis pub/sub requires manual message handling in tests\n        # The important thing is that the publish call doesn't raise\n        await pubsub.unsubscribe(\"application.approved\")\n\n\n# ─── Reject Endpoint Tests ────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\nclass TestRejectApplication:\n    \"\"\"Test PATCH /api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_id}/reject endpoint.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_reject_awaiting_review_pipeline_succeeds(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Rejecting a pipeline in AWAITING_REVIEW status should succeed.\n\n        Asserts:\n          - Response status 200\n          - Response contains pipeline_id and status='REJECTED'\n        \"\"\"\n        response = test_client.patch(\n            f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/reject\"\n        )\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        data = response.json()\n        assert data[\"pipeline_id\"] == str(pipeline_awaiting_review.id)\n        assert data[\"status\"] == \"REJECTED\"\n\n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_reject_transitions_status_to_rejected(\n        self,\n        app_with_overrides: FastAPI,\n        test_db: AsyncSession,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Rejecting should transition pipeline status from any state to REJECTED.\n        \"\"\"\n        async with AsyncClient(\n            transport=ASGITransport(app=app_with_overrides),\n            base_url=\"http://test\",\n        ) as client:\n            response = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/reject\"\n            )\n            assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        # Verify database state\n        result = await test_db.execute(\n            select(ApplicationPipeline).where(\n                ApplicationPipeline.id == pipeline_awaiting_review.id\n            )\n        )\n        pipeline = result.scalar_one_or_none()\n        assert pipeline is not None\n        assert pipeline.status == \"REJECTED\"\n\n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_reject_writes_crm_event(\n        self,\n        app_with_overrides: FastAPI,\n        test_db: AsyncSession,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Rejecting should write a CRM event row for audit trail.\n        \"\"\"\n        async with AsyncClient(\n            transport=ASGITransport(app=app_with_overrides),\n            base_url=\"http://test\",\n        ) as client:\n            response = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/reject\"\n            )\n            assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        # Verify CRM event was logged\n        result = await test_db.execute(\n            select(CRMEvent).where(\n                CRMEvent.pipeline_id == pipeline_awaiting_review.id\n            )\n        )\n        events = result.scalars().all()\n\n        assert len(events) >= 1, \"Expected at least one CRM event after rejection\"\n\n        # Find the rejection event\n        rejection_events = [e for e in events if e.event_type == \"REJECTED\"]\n        assert len(rejection_events) == 1, \"Expected exactly one REJECTED event\"\n\n    def test_reject_nonexistent_pipeline_returns_404(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Rejecting a non-existent pipeline should return 404.\n        \"\"\"\n        fake_pipeline_id = uuid.uuid4()\n        response = test_client.patch(\n            f\"/api/v1/review/application/{fake_pipeline_id}/reject\"\n        )\n        assert response.status_code == 404\n        assert \"not found\" in response.json().get(\"detail\", \"\").lower()\n\n\n# ─── Review Queue Tests ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\nclass TestReviewQueue:\n    \"\"\"Test GET /api/v1/review/queue endpoint.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_queue_returns_awaiting_review_pipelines(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Review queue should return pipelines with status AWAITING_REVIEW.\n        \"\"\"\n        response = test_client.get(\"/api/v1/review/queue\")\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        data = response.json()\n        assert isinstance(data, list)\n        assert len(data) >= 1\n\n        # Find our test pipeline\n        pipeline_ids = [p[\"pipeline_id\"] for p in data]\n        assert str(pipeline_awaiting_review.id) in pipeline_ids\n\n    def test_queue_excludes_non_awaiting_review_pipelines(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n        pipeline_queued: ApplicationPipeline,\n        pipeline_already_approved: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Review queue should NOT include pipelines that are QUEUED or APPROVED.\n        \"\"\"\n        response = test_client.get(\"/api/v1/review/queue\")\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        data = response.json()\n        pipeline_ids = [p[\"pipeline_id\"] for p in data]\n\n        # QUEUED and APPROVED pipelines should not appear\n        assert str(pipeline_queued.id) not in pipeline_ids\n        assert str(pipeline_already_approved.id) not in pipeline_ids\n\n    def test_queue_returns_empty_when_no_awaiting_review(\n        self,\n        test_client: TestClient,\n        pipeline_queued: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Review queue should return empty list when no pipelines are awaiting review.\n        \"\"\"\n        response = test_client.get(\"/api/v1/review/queue\")\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n\n        data = response.json()\n        # Only QUEUED pipeline exists, which should not be in queue\n        assert str(pipeline_queued.id) not in [p[\"pipeline_id\"] for p in data]\n\n\n# ─── Full Integration Flow Tests ──────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n\nclass TestFullApprovalFlow:\n    \"\"\"\n    End-to-end integration tests for the complete approval workflow.\n\n    Contract: HYPHA-TESTS.md\n    \"full integration: create application → approve → verify state transition\"\n    \"\"\"\n\n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_full_flow_create_approve_verify(\n        self,\n        app_with_overrides: FastAPI,\n        test_db: AsyncSession,\n        test_candidate: Candidate,\n        test_job: DiscoveredJob,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Full integration test: create application → approve → verify transition.\n\n        Steps:\n          1. Create a new ApplicationPipeline in AWAITING_REVIEW state\n          2. POST to approve endpoint\n          3. Verify pipeline status is now APPROVED\n          4. Verify CRM event was logged\n        \"\"\"\n        # Step 1: Create pipeline directly in test database\n        pipeline = ApplicationPipeline(\n            id=uuid.uuid4(),\n            candidate_id=test_candidate.id,\n            job_id=test_job.id,\n            status=\"AWAITING_REVIEW\",\n            current_step=\"outreach_compose\",\n        )\n        test_db.add(pipeline)\n        await test_db.commit()\n        await test_db.refresh(pipeline)\n        pipeline_id = pipeline.id\n\n        # Step 2: Approve via API\n        async with AsyncClient(\n            transport=ASGITransport(app=app_with_overrides),\n            base_url=\"http://test\",\n        ) as client:\n            response = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_id}/approve\"\n            )\n            assert response.status_code == 200\n            assert response.json()[\"status\"] == \"APPROVED\"\n\n        # Step 3: Verify pipeline status in database\n        result = await test_db.execute(\n            select(ApplicationPipeline).where(ApplicationPipeline.id == pipeline_id)\n        )\n        updated_pipeline = result.scalar_one_or_none()\n        assert updated_pipeline is not None\n        assert updated_pipeline.status == \"APPROVED\"\n\n        # Step 4: Verify CRM event exists\n        crm_result = await test_db.execute(\n            select(CRMEvent).where(CRMEvent.pipeline_id == pipeline_id)\n        )\n        crm_events = crm_result.scalars().all()\n        assert len(crm_events) >= 1\n\n        approval_event = next(\n            (e for e in crm_events if e.event_type == \"APPROVED_FOR_SUBMISSION\"),\n            None,\n        )\n        assert approval_event is not None\n        assert approval_event.candidate_id == test_candidate.id\n        assert approval_event.job_id == test_job.id\n\n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_approval_is_idempotent_check(\n        self,\n        app_with_overrides: FastAPI,\n        test_db: AsyncSession,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Once approved, re-approval should fail with 422.\n\n        This ensures the state machine is respected.\n        \"\"\"\n        async with AsyncClient(\n            transport=ASGITransport(app=app_with_overrides),\n            base_url=\"http://test\",\n        ) as client:\n            # First approval should succeed\n            response1 = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/approve\"\n            )\n            assert response1.status_code == 200\n            assert response1.json()[\"status\"] == \"APPROVED\"\n\n            # Second approval should fail\n            response2 = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/approve\"\n            )\n            assert response2.status_code == 422\n\n    @pytest.mark.asyncio\n    async def test_queue_updates_after_approval(\n        self,\n        app_with_overrides: FastAPI,\n        test_db: AsyncSession,\n        pipeline_awaiting_review: ApplicationPipeline,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        After approval, the pipeline should no longer appear in the review queue.\n        \"\"\"\n        async with AsyncClient(\n            transport=ASGITransport(app=app_with_overrides),\n            base_url=\"http://test\",\n        ) as client:\n            # Check queue before approval\n            queue_before = await client.get(\"/api/v1/review/queue\")\n            assert queue_before.status_code == 200\n            ids_before = [p[\"pipeline_id\"] for p in queue_before.json()]\n            assert str(pipeline_awaiting_review.id) in ids_before\n\n            # Approve\n            approve_response = await client.patch(\n                f\"/api/v1/review/application/{pipeline_awaiting_review.id}/approve\"\n            )\n            assert approve_response.status_code == 200\n\n            # Check queue after approval\n            queue_after = await client.get(\"/api/v1/review/queue\")\n            assert queue_after.status_code == 200\n            ids_after = [p[\"pipeline_id\"] for p in queue_after.json()]\n            assert str(pipeline_awaiting_review.id) not in ids_after\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}}
