{"t":"2026-05-28T03:05:00.730Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_015p97SJAyKRQ66AQdZC2BwT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I see the events stream test only uses the `User` model which doesn't have ARRAY columns. For my test I need models with ARRAY columns (Candidate has `target_locations`, `excluded_companies`, etc.). \n\nThe issue is SQLite doesn't support PostgreSQL's ARRAY type. I need to either:\n1. Use PostgreSQL for testing (requires a running PostgreSQL server)\n2. Mock the database operations\n3. Use an alternative approach that doesn't need ARRAY columns\n\nLooking at HYPHA-TESTS.md: \"Test uses in-memory SQLite for database\". This is a challenge since the models use PostgreSQL-specific types.\n\nLet me check the scheduler test to see how it handles this:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":901,"cache_read_input_tokens":105989,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":901,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1a6c245-4572-4816-9d85-5634565bd455","uuid":"31936534-7923-4ea8-a527-f48cef847111"}}
